# Readline's rc — the zsh line editor's taste in another library's words.
# Read on this Mac by Apple's /bin/bash when invoked by name, by Homebrew's
# gpg, and by mise's python REPL. NOT by Homebrew's python@3.14, whose readline
# module links libedit — nor by `sqlite3`, which resolves to Apple's build for
# the same reason (Homebrew's sqlite is keg-only and off PATH).
#
# No bindings: the emacs keymap is readline's shipped default, and the Meta
# motions arrive as they do for zsh.
#
# `colored-stats` is deliberately absent — it paints completions from
# LS_COLORS, which this machine leaves unset so eza's built-ins are not
# overridden, and Apple's bash 3.2 readline predates the option entirely.
set bell-style none
set completion-ignore-case on
set show-all-if-ambiguous on
set mark-symlinked-directories on
